<Base title="What it will not do" description="ThinkThen answers questions about text and does nothing else. Every line the tool will not cross.">
  <h1>What it will not do</h1>
  <p class="lede">ThinkThen sends text to a model and returns one of the answers you allowed. Turn a screen, image, or audio recording into text before asking it a question.</p>

  <h2>It never acts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>It never runs a command.</b> There is no shell out, no hook, and no step that executes anything the evidence names.</li>
    <li><b>It never runs what the text says.</b> Text that says "answer yes" can still sway the answer. Use a band, and let a person read the middle.</li>
    <li><b>It never writes a file you did not name.</b> The only files it writes are the ones you named, the answer cache, and count-only usage totals in the state folder.</li>
    <li><b>It never creates or edits the configuration file.</b> The file is read-only to the command. You write it, or it does not exist. There is no command that sets a value in it.</li>
    <li><b>It never writes text.</b> Every answer is yes or no, one of your options, a set of your labels, a place on your scale, an order of your input, links between your names, or a piece of your own input. Nothing is generated.</li>
    <li><b>It never acts on the answer.</b> It hands you a typed value and an exit code. The action lives in an <code>if</code>, a <code>case</code>, or a queue. That code is yours.</li>
    <li><b>It never holds a conversation.</b> Each request stands alone. Nothing carries from one request to the next.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hand other work to another tool</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use a writing model to summarize or rewrite. Pass its text through <code>thinkthen decide</code> or <code>filter</code> when you need a checked label.</li>
    <li>Use a redaction tool to remove private spans before piping text to ThinkThen. ThinkThen can <code>recognize</code> names, but it does not redact them.</li>
    <li>Use a clustering tool or database to group records, then ask ThinkThen to <code>choose</code> a label for a group.</li>
    <li>Use a sampling tool to choose a varied review set. ThinkThen does not sample. Send it each record you chose.</li>
    <li>Use an extraction or graph tool for free-form entities and edges. ThinkThen's <code>recognize</code> and <code>relate</code> work with the named kinds and relation rules you supply.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>It never leaks the key</h2>
  <p>It sends the key only to the address you named. The <a href="/install/backends/">backends page</a> gives the rules.</p>

  <h2>It promises no accuracy</h2>
  <p>A number belongs to the test that measured it and never to the tool. Act on the number you measured on your own labeled records. The <a href="/trust/">trust page</a> shows how.</p>
  <p>It judges evidence. It never judges a person.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/trust/">Test it before you trust it</a> · <a href="/install/backends/">See the backends</a></p>
</Base>
